WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.134
-Welcome back, everyone.

00:00:02.134 --> 00:00:03.803
I am hanging out with
the one and only Tracy Morgan!

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:06.772
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.772 --> 00:00:08.974
Currently the star
of "Coming 2 America."

00:00:08.974 --> 00:00:12.979
We're about to face off
in a game called "Box of Lies."

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:15.815
-♪ Box of lies, box of lies ♪

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:18.484
♪ Box of lies, box of lies ♪

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:21.253
♪ Box of lies ♪
-Yeah.

00:00:21.253 --> 00:00:22.788
I can't even look at you.
You make me laugh.

00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:25.491
Here's how it works.
We have nine mystery boxes

00:00:25.491 --> 00:00:27.827
containing objects
no one has ever seen before.

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:30.663
On your turn, you pick a box,
take out the object,

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:32.298
and describe it
to your opponent,

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:35.334
and they have to guess if you're
lying or telling the truth.

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.837
We'll play three rounds.

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.605
All right, Tracy,
you pick the first box.

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:42.041
-You want me to pick that box?
-Yeah, I want you --

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:44.077
-Well, then that box
is being picked.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:46.612
[ Laughter ]
Ahh!

00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:48.148
I pick 5.
-All right.

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:50.549
[ Cheers and applause ]
You pick 5.

00:00:50.549 --> 00:00:53.352
-I hope there's something
in here to cure my sciatica.

00:00:53.352 --> 00:00:55.554
[ Laughter ]
-Pick 5.

00:00:55.554 --> 00:00:57.223
Here we go.
I'm not looking.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.558
I can't see nothing.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.092
All I can see is just your face.

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:03.562
So you got to play
either you're lying already

00:01:03.562 --> 00:01:05.464
or, like, maybe
you don't think that's funny.

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:07.132
See, that's the tricky thing
about this game.

00:01:07.132 --> 00:01:08.968
Already you can be
playing the game

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.537
before you even started
playing the game.

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:13.072
-So I got to tell you
what it is, right?

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:14.974
-Yeah, describe it to me.

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:17.644
-It's a drink.
It's one of these fruity drinks.

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:18.778
-Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.346
-It's a fruity drink.
-Okay.

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:22.916
-With a little munchkin
on the top with a Yankee hat.

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:25.285
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:27.921
-Fruity drink with a munchkin --
-Looks like my cousin Russell.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.289
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:31.524
You know exactly --
It's from McDonald's.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:32.592
-Eh?

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:35.227
-Russ love these drinks
from McDonald's.

00:01:35.227 --> 00:01:38.531
-Oh, so you're talking about
a Shamrock Shake, baby?

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:42.568
-You know what?
This a Shamrock Shake?

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:46.072
-Yeah.
-It's a Shamrock Shake.

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:48.073
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.073 --> 00:01:50.643
-Wait, hold on, hold on,
hold on, hold on, hold on.

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:55.080
So you think it's a --
it's a Shamrock Shake.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.116
Your cousin Russell --

00:01:57.116 --> 00:01:59.718
You've seen Russell
with this object?

00:01:59.718 --> 00:02:01.587
-Russell stayed with them.
-He stayed with McDonald's

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:02.821
all the way through --
-Shamrock Shake.

00:02:02.821 --> 00:02:04.390
Yeah, he'd smoke weed,
and then he'd drink it.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:07.660
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, gosh.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.695
[ Sighs ]
Gosh.

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:12.164
-Roll the dice, baby.
-I know, I got you, I got you.

00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:13.399
I got you.
I'm gonna say...

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:17.002
[ Drum roll ]

00:02:17.002 --> 00:02:19.004
You lie.

00:02:19.004 --> 00:02:21.707
-You know what?
I ain't lying, brother.

00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:23.442
-[ Laughing ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:23.442 --> 00:02:27.680
♪♪

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.281
-Oh!

00:02:29.281 --> 00:02:31.283
He was wearing a little
Yankee hat, there you go.

00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:33.519
[ Laughs ]

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:34.520
All right, buddy.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:35.621
I thought Russell got me
on that one.

00:02:35.621 --> 00:02:37.390
All right,
it's my turn to pick a box.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.691
Here we go.
Which one?

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:40.527
Up here.
Something close to me?

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:42.128
-1! 1!

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:44.596
-The deuce, the deuce,
the deuce.

00:02:44.596 --> 00:02:46.833
-Jump on it.
-[ Groans ]

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:49.702
-Jump on it.
-[ Grunting ]

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:52.171
-So heavy.
-Right. Okay.

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:53.906
-See what I'm saying, dude?
-Yeah.

00:02:53.906 --> 00:02:55.307
-I'm in there already.
I'm playing around,

00:02:55.307 --> 00:02:56.876
jumping rope,
I'm Double Dutching

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.444
in your head right now, dude.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.746
I'm like...
♪ Miss Lucy had a ♪

00:03:00.746 --> 00:03:03.549
♪♪

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:05.518
-I got to meditate
and go into my powers.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:08.254
-Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:11.224
-My Spock powers.
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:13.959
-I'm a Vulcan.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:19.398
From the first "Star Trek."
-Okay.

00:03:19.398 --> 00:03:22.901
It's, uh, Baby Yoda.
-Baby Yoda?

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:25.438
-Yeah, and there's money
coming out of his mouth.

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:27.607
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:29.775
-Yoda don't even like money.

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:31.076
-That's probably
why he's throwing it up.

00:03:31.076 --> 00:03:32.645
-He owe Luke some money.

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:35.148
Why you think him
and Darth Vader had problems?

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:38.284
-So you think I'm tell --
-I think you lying.

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:40.153
You might even be habitual.

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:42.088
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:45.091
-You're correct -- I was lying.
You got it.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:47.126
You got it, man.
Look at this thing.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:48.494
♪♪

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:49.762
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.997
Yeah, you know me too well.
All right.

00:03:51.997 --> 00:03:55.468
Let's do one more round.
This one's worth 10,000 points.

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:57.503
Whoever wins this
wins the whole thing.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:00.073
Tracy, pick a box.
-I'm asking my squad.

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:02.241
Which one should I pick, y'all?
-9!

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:04.677
-6!
-Number 1!

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.278
-All right, here we go.
-I picked 4.

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:09.282
-Cuatro.
-Pretty heavy.

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:12.919
-Ooh.
Sounded heavy.

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:14.386
-You ready?
-Whenever you're ready,

00:04:14.386 --> 00:04:16.322
tell me what's in your box,
dude.

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:19.558
-Well, I'm gonna tell you --
Oh, man, this is dope.

00:04:19.558 --> 00:04:22.461
-[ Chuckles ]
This is dope.

00:04:22.461 --> 00:04:24.163
All right.
Look at this.

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:26.398
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.398 --> 00:04:29.669
Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:32.738
-You ready?
-I was born ready, man.

00:04:32.738 --> 00:04:35.508
-I think it's a...

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:37.610
It's a cake.
-Yeah, gotcha.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.979
-On a young
Arnold Schwarzenegger.

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:41.447
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:43.215
And it say,
"Don't skip leg day."

00:04:43.215 --> 00:04:45.885
-Okay.
That's what he always said.

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:47.987
So you think it's a cake --
You think that what is

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:51.457
in your box is a cake with a
young Arnold Schwarzenegger?

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:54.326
I'm saying what, teens, 20s?

00:04:54.326 --> 00:04:56.863
Mr. Universe type of jam?

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:58.964
-Late 20s.
-Late 20s.

00:04:58.964 --> 00:05:00.333
-Yeah.
-Yeah, and underneath that,

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:03.336
it says --
-I can tell by his calf muscles.

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:05.938
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:08.040
I need to ask you a question.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:11.143
-Yeah?
-Am I lying, or am I not?

00:05:11.143 --> 00:05:12.978
[ Drum roll ]

00:05:12.978 --> 00:05:15.447
-He means business, man.
It's for all the money.

00:05:15.447 --> 00:05:17.183
For all the marbles.

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:21.721
[ Drum roll ]
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:26.792
You lying.

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:30.062
-[ Clears throat ]

00:05:30.062 --> 00:05:31.998
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:34.067
-What in the what?

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:36.735
"Don't skip leg day."
Gosh darn it!

00:05:36.735 --> 00:05:38.805
Man, you're good!
You are good!

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:41.106
The best right there!
Tracy Morgan, everybody!

00:05:41.106 --> 00:05:43.142
His new movie,
"Coming 2 America,"

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:46.112
begins streaming
on Amazon Prime Video tomorrow.

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:49.648
The one and only, the best in
the biz right there, come on.

00:05:49.648 --> 00:05:51.017
That's what I'm talking about.

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:52.752
Stick around for more
"Tonight Show," everybody.

